{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408719-should-mundane-superior-craft-just-be-projects","id":1408719,"title":"Should Mundane Superior Craft Just be Projects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-17T07:55:55-07:00","id":1408719,"title":"Should Mundane Superior Craft Just be Projects?","content":"Okay so for crafting a sword, you can pretty much do that as a single person with a small workshop and fairly readily available materials. Building a ship, or a manse, or a wall to fend off northern barbarians, much less so. A single person may be the architect for it, the designer, but 99% of the physical work is being done by many people, and a lot of the materials for it are custom orders or hard to get. It seems to me that the craft roll to make a fortress or a manse or whatever should be to make the plans, and the projects \u201csystem\u201d should be used to actually do it.<br /> <br /> Hopefully there\u2019s some kind of projects hack in Crucible of Legends or something.<br /> <br /> Does that make more sense? Is there something I\u2019m missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T08:40:09-07:00","id":1408725,"title":"","content":"I'm 100% with you there. Could also do pretty well with some of those &quot;just use Workings for Projects&quot; hacks. A bangin' plan could be Means, or any of the other myriad bonuses, or maybe you could sub in a roll or two for teamwork between the characters designing, supplying, and overseeing the execution.<br /> <br /> Adjacently related Craft Hack- in the manuscript for the new Aberrant, there is a concept of &quot;paradigm shift&quot; which models how you can trickle down your super genious to the general population, and in universe is how they have the proliferation of grav-crystals and super internet etc. Basically, you do a craft project to make the original, and then do a whole other craft project to refactor it be partially completed without direct intervention of the Crafter, and then finally, you can do another project to make it so that it becomes a new concept of engineering/material science that can be used by anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T08:52:56-07:00","id":1408727,"title":"","content":"Personally, I treat superior mundane craft as <i>both</i> a Craft project and a Bureaucracy-style project. Specifically, during the time period necessary before any rolls can be made, I assume that the primary problems then are logistical, and have failure conditions pop up that require resolution before the work can continue. Then, once the interval is finished, I assume that basically all the parts are on hand and the majority of the &quot;grunt work&quot; is finished, the stuff that requires a big labor force, and that the Craft rolls now represent the crafter putting everything together and doing the critical bits that transform what was a big pile of stone into an actual <i>wall</i>, or four walls and a roof into a palace, or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:13:45-07:00","id":1408729,"title":"","content":"I'm with Kelly. In many ways it's really both, and it's how I've played it, system or not (the book mentions that this is work that must be done before crafting, but isn't very emphatic or clear).<br /> <br /> We just need an actual project management widget (and let's be frank at its core it's going to be a simple or extended roll with a goal, as that's a decent way to cover extensive tasks of any sort).<br /> The separation between the two won't always be smooth, especially when you factor in the acceleration/decceleration charms, but it should be easy to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:49:47-07:00","id":1408737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408719-should-mundane-superior-craft-just-be-projects?p=1408729#post1408729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We just need an actual project management widget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried making one myself once but never ultimately settled on if it was good or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348783-codifying-leadership\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348783-codifying-leadership\"> Codifying Leadership - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348783-codifying-leadership\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348783-codifying-leadership </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I wanted to make a simple system that slots into the current leadership system and charms that will help codify what&rsquo;s possible, and give some guidelines for projects. I&rsquo;d like to start by introducing a few concepts. Committed Resource Dots Resources doesn&rsquo;t represent a total amount of wealth, but rather a revenue stream. This means that spending resource dots doesn&rsquo;t make a lot of sense, you don&rsquo;t give up some of your hourly wage to buy things. Instead resource dots will be committed at the start of each project and will be unavailable for other projects for the duration. The number of </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T10:38:32-07:00","id":1408743,"title":"","content":"As a player: No. I want my damn 2 WhP!<br /> <br /> As a ST: Yes. Full support.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> In Dynasty of Dovak, the worker's district of Dovak was raised by a Deathknight. We made it a Project to get the raw materials and labour together, then a Superior Craft to rebuild the city. But if I wasn't playing an architect, I'd just have done it as a project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-17-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T11:14:11-07:00","id":1408749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408719-should-mundane-superior-craft-just-be-projects?p=1408743#post1408743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player: No. I want my damn 2 WhP!<br /> <br /> As a ST: Yes. Full support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah maybe use a project as the prerequisite time kind of thing, then start making craft rolls once the project is done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:59:13-07:00","id":1408772,"title":"","content":"My two main issues are:<br /> <br /> 1) The 3e core project system is very meh. In fact, saying that you have to a project to support mundane Superior Crafting basically would only exist for STs throwing obstacles into your way if they feel like it.<br /> <br /> 2) It's just something that would mostly exist for Charms to get rid of (it's not like we're tracking on the PC Craft stuff for NPCs). I want my Exalts to be capable of legendary mythological feats, including Craft. This means things like Hercules soloing the earthworks to reroute a river. Which means it would just turn into one more Charm to buy to remove a barrier to doing awesome things, instead of a Charm that makes you feel more awesome (which I know is fairly subjective).<br /> <br /> Hopefully between Crucible of Legends and Essence we'll see a more robust Projects system that can unify a few related but currently disparate subsystems, but as it stands I wouldn't want to have to deal with this hoop if I was playing an Exalt focused on Crafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}